# Study: noise and offset

Order 2, N=1024, Cs=1 pF/side, c1=0.25, OTA white 6.9 nV/√Hz, 1/f corner 631 kHz (pthomas sky130 measurement). `lf gain` = input referral of slow OTA errors: 1 for bottom-plate SC (expected), 5.30 = pessimistic bound. Each output = mean of K consecutive sub-conversions; rms over 24 outputs. Effective resolution = log2(4.096 V / rms). Mean = residual offset (the ~−2 µV floor is deterministic quantisation error at the 0.1·VREF test input). MCP3421 column: its no-missing-codes bits at that rate (its noise is 1.5 µV at 3.75 SPS).

